**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`

**How to implement.** An experiment references its setup by name and revision, and the descriptor list goes (001 §J 'Experiments reference setups (name + revision). The ElementDescriptor list becomes the slot list'; the S8.2 brief: 'Experiment.setup : ElementDescriptor list becomes a setup reference (name + revision). ElementDescriptor, ElementBinding and PlacementSummary go wherever a slot carries the same facts. Experiments keep their captured-snapshot meaning through the setup revision: editing a setup that an experiment uses mints the next revision'; .spec-md §3.15: copying experiments brings their setups). This is one step because the record field's type changes every consumer at once. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Experiments.fs`. (a) `ElementBinding`, `PlacementSummary` and `ElementDescriptor` (`Experiments.fs:ElementBinding`, `:PlacementSummary`, `:ElementDescriptor`) are deleted with their members (`versionRefOpt`, step 137's `entryReferenceOpt`): a slot carries their facts, its placement the kind, position, R1 / R2 / R3 and library binding and its content the item (step 256). (b) `VariedElement` (`Experiments.fs:VariedElement`) gains `label : ElementLabel` after `elementId`: the varied slot's label as the experiment captured it, so a row outlives the slot. (c) `Experiment.setup` (`Experiments.fs:Experiment`) becomes `SetupReference` (step 255), the setup and revision the experiment was recorded over. `variedDescriptor`, `detectorDescriptorOpt`, `versionRefs` and step 137's `libraryReferences` are deleted; `variedLabel` answers `varied`'s `label`, blank for a dark line; `description` keeps its varied text and renders a dark line `Dark line on setup <setup.describe>, capture <measurement.label>`. (d) `commit (setup : SetupReference) (c : ExperimentCollection)` (`Experiments.fs:commit`) builds the `VariedElement` with `draft.elementLabel`; nothing else in it changes. (e) Step 221's `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` moves to `Setups.fs` (below). (f) The module doc becomes one to three lines: the editable experiments, each a run recorded over one revision of a kit setup (spec 0050 S8.2); every doc that names a descriptor, a binding or a captured chain says what stays true. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Lifecycle.fs`: `VersionRef` (`Lifecycle.fs:VersionRef`) and step 137's `VersionRef.entryReference` are deleted, their one reader `ElementBinding` going (step 65 kept `VersionRef` for that binding alone); a fixture of `SampleProxyTests` or `MaterialProxyTests` that still names it builds the `SampleVersionId` or `MaterialVersionId` it wrapped instead, every fact keeping its assertions. (3) `Setups.fs`, after step 258's members: `type Setup with member this.pinFor (experiments : Experiment list) : PinState`, `VersionPinned` when an experiment's `setup` is this setup's `reference` and `VersionUnpinned` otherwise; `type Experiment with member this.slotsIn (setups : Setup list) : Result<SetupSlot list, SetupError>`, the slots of the setup its reference names at its revision (`slotsAt`), `UnknownSetupErr` naming the reference when the list holds no setup of that name; and `type Experiment with static member itemsUsedBy (experiments : Experiment list) (setups : Setup list) (items : Item list) : Result<Item list, SetupError>`, resolving referenced revisions and explicit slot ItemIds; a missing setup/revision MUST answer its slotsIn error and a missing piece SetupItemReferenceErr (UnknownKitItemErr _), never an empty successful list. The Ok items MUST retain supplied item order and uniqueness. S6 physical-identity semantics MUST survive the descriptor retirement. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`: `detectorKindOf (library : LibraryProxy) (slots : SetupSlot list) : DetectorKind` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:detectorKindOf`) reads the first `Detector` slot's placement binding (a `DetectorItem`'s kind) where it read the detector descriptor's, `Intensity` otherwise, so its rule is unchanged; `loadAndValidate` (`ExperimentDataLoad.fs:loadAndValidate`) takes `(slots : SetupSlot list)` after the data proxy, the caller resolving the experiment's slots. The module doc becomes one to three lines. (5) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentCollectionStore.fs`: `ExperimentCollectionSnapshot` (`ExperimentCollectionStore.fs:ExperimentCollectionSnapshot`) gains `setups : Setup list`, the setups its experiments reference, and its doc names them. (6) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitLibrary.fs`: `KitLibraryError` (step 139) gains `KitLibrarySetupErr of SetupError`, rendered `the setup could not be used: <e.describe>`; every match over the error (its captions in `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, step 173) gains the case. (7) Storage. (a) `schema/experiment.schema.json` (step 146): `experiment.setup` becomes an object holding exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character) and `revision` (a positive integer); the rest is unchanged, so a version-1 file of the descriptor shape is refused by its schema. (b) `KitContentFiles.fs`: `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` (step 149) reads `this.kit.proxy.readSetups ()` (step 260) and answers `KitLibrarySetupErr` of `experiment.slotsIn setups`'s error, writing nothing, when the kit lacks the referenced revision; otherwise it writes the experiment with `writeExperiment`. It snapshots nothing: the setup's versions were snapshotted when it was recorded (step 260), so a written experiment never references a version or a revision the kit lacks. (c) `KitContext.copyExperimentsFrom` (steps 224, 227) brings the setups its experiments reference, its read-then-write order and its report kept. After the kept experiments (224 (b)) it reads `source.proxy.readSetups ()`; the kept setups are those the kept experiments reference, in first-reference order, and an experiment whose revision the source lacks answers `KitLibrarySetupErr` before anything is written. The used items are `Experiment.itemsUsedBy` of the kept experiments over the kept setups and the source's items. Each kept setup is mapped through the item rows: in every revision, a slot holding an item that a row maps onto a kit item (`MapOntoKitItem id`, step 221) holds `id`; an added item keeps its id (step 221 adds it under it). It reads `this.proxy.readSetups ()`: a mapped setup equal to the kit's setup whose `name.fileStem` equals its own (ignoring case) is not written; one whose name the kit holds with other content is renamed `name.nextFreeAmong` (step 255) the kit's names and those given so far, and the kept experiments that reference it reference the new name at the same revision; every other is written as it is. The closure (224 (c), 240) walks the mapped setups' `libraryReferences` (step 260) followed by the added items'. The writes are the snapshots, the lab files, the added items, then each setup to write through `writeSetup`, then the experiments. `ExperimentCopyReport` (step 224) gains `setups : Setup list` after `items`, each setup written as written. No merge, deduplication across names or other option is added. (8) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) `model.experimentSetup` and `descriptorBinding` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:experimentSetup`, `:descriptorBinding`) are deleted. (b) `ExpCommit` with a capture: the table's slots are `model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems)`; the setup is `active.revisedWith slots (active.pinFor model.experimentCollection.experiments)` (step 256 and (3)) when `activeSetupOpt` is `Some active`, and otherwise the `Setup.create (SetupName.firstFree <the names of kitSetups>) slots model.kitSetups` (step 255), which no held name refuses. Unless it equals `active` it is recorded through `recordSetup` (step 260); then the collection commits over its `reference` and the experiment is recorded as step 152 records it. A refusal of either keeps the collection, `kitSetups` and `activeSetupOpt` and sets `kitStatus` to `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`; on success `kitSetups` holds the setup in place of its name's and `activeSetupOpt` is `Some` it. So editing a setup an experiment uses mints the next revision, and the earlier experiment keeps its own. (c) The attach validation (`AttachDataFileTo` and `loadKit`'s, steps 135, 152) passes `loadAndValidate` the experiment's `slotsIn model.kitSetups`; an experiment whose setup the kit lacks gets `AttachedFileValidationError` of the error's `describe`. (d) `CopyChosenExperiments` (steps 225, 227) also reads `model.kit.proxy.readSetups ()` after the items and passes them to the content function (step 260), so the copied setups are the window's; its `Error e` is step 225's. (9) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SolverHandoffView.fs`: `unspecifiedElements` and `handoffSetupCaption` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:validateExperiment`'s checks) read the experiment's slots in `collection.setups` (`slotsIn`) in light order (`SetupSlot.inLightOrder`, step 257): a slot is specified when it holds an item or its placement is bound, the `Sample` slots being the unknowns, and the caption lists `<role.text> [<tag>]`; an experiment whose setup the collection lacks is `UnspecifiedElements` naming the reference. `validateExperiment` and `buildRows` (`SolverHandoffView.fs:buildRows`) take `(setups : Setups.Setup list)` after the data proxy, `initSolverHandoff` passing `collection.setups`, and read the detector through `ExperimentDataLoad.detectorKindOf library <the slots>`. (10) `AGENTS.md`, a new gotcha after 'An experiment runs on the light's real path': **The table is the active setup.** Its elements are the setup's slots (`Setups.fs`), the source first; a slot holds a kit item or nothing, and a dial-mounted item records its raw dial reading. An experiment references its setup by name and revision, and recording a changed table over a revision an experiment references mints the next revision (`Lifecycle.decideVersioning`). Nothing else in the file changes. Tests. `ExperimentProxyTests`: its `desc`, `placementOf`, `glassPlateBinding`, `srcSetup` and `polSetup` fixtures become test-local `SetupReference`s (`Bench` revision 1, `Bench` revision 2, `Dark` revision 1), and the E1 / E2 / E3 experiments reference them with labelled varied elements; `commit APPENDS a new experiment and then keeps editing it (no duplicate on re-commit)`, `editing the draft after add updates the stored experiment in place`, `newDraft after add lets a second commit APPEND a distinct experiment`, `edit loads an experiment into the draft for re-editing`, `remove deletes the experiment and clears the draft when it was being edited`, `an experiment description mentions the element, the variable, and the capture`, `E3 is an empty dark line — nothing varied, still describable` (the description names `'Dark' revision 1`), `E1 and E2 describe their varied element, variable and capture`, `attachDataFile binds one data attachment per experiment`, `copied experiments keep their ids unless the kit holds them, and a clash takes the next free id` and `a STUB proxy of the same shape drives the same listing logic` keep their assertions over them. `E1 carries the ordered chain incl. the detector, with the varied polarizer identified within it` becomes `E1 references its setup revision and names its varied polarizer with its label`: E1's `setup` is `Bench` revision 1 and its varied element `lp2` labelled `Linear polarizer #4` varying R1. `committing from a scene captures the ordered chain including the detector kind` becomes `committing references the setup revision and the varied slot with its label`: `commit` of `Bench` revision 2 after `chooseElement` holds that reference and `lp2`'s label. `the items an experiment uses are its explicit physical ids, each once` becomes `the items an experiment uses are those its setup revision's slots hold, each once`: of the items Laser, QZ, QZ2 and CPL1, an experiment over a setup whose source slot holds Laser and whose sample slot holds QZ uses exactly Laser and QZ, in that order; two experiments over it name Laser once; an experiment whose setup holds no item, uses none; a missing setup or item MUST return its typed error. `E2 is constructible without a sample (source + two polarizers + detector)`, `versionRefs collects the versioned bindings of the setup (samples yes, presets no)`, `pinning an experiment's bound sample version BLOCKS removal of that sample`, `editing a PINNED sample version mints the next version instead of rewriting it` and `an experiment references the library versions its setup binds, each once` are deleted: an experiment no longer holds elements or bindings, and the setup's references and the samples' pins are `KitContentFileJsonTests`' (step 260) and `SampleProxyTests`' (step 65). `LifecycleTests`: `version ref distinguishes a material version from a sample version` is deleted with `VersionRef`. `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` (steps 148, 260): its E1 / E2 / E3 reference test-local setups written through `writeSetup`; `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments` becomes `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving their setup references, optional shapes and data attachments`; `writing an experiment again replaces its kit file`, `deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others`, `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file` and `a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing` keep their assertions over them. `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146): its E1 references `Bench` revision 2 and E3 `Dark` revision 1; `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text` and `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` keep their assertions; `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds` also refuses `experiment.setup` as an array and with `revision` 0. `KitLibraryTests` (step 149): `recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file` becomes `recording an experiment over a setup revision the kit holds writes its file and snapshots nothing of its own`: with a setup recorded first, `recordExperiment` writes the experiment and `listSnapshots` holds only what `recordSetup` wrote; `a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing` records a setup binding a test-local GUID through `recordSetup`, with the same assertions; `a read-only kit records nothing` records the setup before reopening read-only, so `recordExperiment` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`; `every kit library error renders its condition and its payload` covers `KitLibrarySetupErr`; and `an experiment over a setup revision the kit lacks records nothing`: an experiment over `Bench` revision 2 in a kit holding `Bench` at revision 1 answers `KitLibrarySetupErr (UnknownSetupRevisionErr _)` and `readExperiments` answers `[]`. `ExperimentCopyTests` (steps 224, 227): the source's setups are recorded through `recordSetup` before its experiments: E1's setup `Bench` binds `PresetIds.source600` and `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` and its slots hold `Laser600` and `ML`, E2's `Plate` binds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and holds `QZ`, and E3's `Dark` binds nothing; every existing fact keeps its assertions and also finds each copied experiment's setup in the target. `a copy brings the setups its experiments reference, their items mapped onto the kit's`: copying [E1] into an empty target writes `Bench.setup-json`, whose slots hold `Laser600` and `ML` under their ids; over a target whose `ML` is mapped by model and label onto a kit item of another id, the copied `Bench` holds that id in every revision. `a copied setup the kit holds with the same content is not written again, and one with other content takes the next free name`: over a target already holding the same `Bench`, nothing is written for it and the report's `setups` is `[]`; over a target holding a `Bench` of other slots, the copy is `Bench (2).setup-json` and the copied E1 references `Bench (2)` at its revision. `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests`: `requestedWavelengthsOf: a wavelength-sweep experiment requests its range; a dark line is fixed` builds its dark line over a test-local reference. `SetupTests`: `an experiment pins the revision it references, and its slots resolve through the kit's setups`: over the setups `Bench` (revision 2, one history record) and `Plate`, an experiment over `Bench` revision 1 resolves the history record's slots, one over revision 2 the current slots, one over `Gone` answers `UnknownSetupErr` and one over `Bench` revision 3 `UnknownSetupRevisionErr`; `Bench.pinFor` is `VersionPinned` for the revision-2 experiment and `VersionUnpinned` for only the revision-1 one. `SetupModelTests` (step 260), over its folder kit: `a commit on a table that is no setup yet records it as the first free setup and references it`: with a linear polarizer added and chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), `ExpCommit` writes `Setup 1.setup-json` and `E1.experiment-json`, the experiment references `Setup 1` revision 1 and `activeSetupOpt` is `Setup 1`. `a commit over a changed table whose revision an experiment references mints the next revision, and the earlier experiment keeps its own`: after that commit, the polarizer turned (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 30.0)`, it being selected), then `ExpNew`, `ExpChooseElement` of it and `ExpCommit` give `Setup 1` revision 2 with revision 1 in its history, the new experiment references revision 2 and E1 still references revision 1, as the kit files read back. `a commit over a changed table no experiment references changes the setup in place`: a table created as `Bench` (`CreateSetup`), turned, then committed keeps `Bench` at revision 1 holding the turned slots, with no history. `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 225, 228): the source kits' experiments are recorded over recorded setups, and `copying the chosen experiments brings them into the kit and the window, and closes the source`, `choosing experiments lists the items they use, each at its default` and `the user's choice for an item is kept and copied` keep their assertions. UI tests: `InverseConstructorTests` (step 152): `committed experiments and their attachments are kept in the kit and reopen with it` and `a commit, an attach and a removal write the kit's experiment files` also find `Setup 1.setup-json`; `opening a kit re-validates an attachment whose data is unchanged` and `opening a kit flags an attachment whose data changed since attach or is missing` write each experiment's setup before it; `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path` reads its detector kind from the experiment's setup slots. `SolverHandoffWindowTests`: `snapshotOf` carries the committed model's `kitSetups`; `an unbound non-sample element yields UnspecifiedElements` finds the role texts `Source` and `Detector 1` in its reason; `the detector kind selects the ellipsometric load path` and `init validates every received experiment and carries the collection name` keep their assertions; and `an experiment whose setup the collection lacks yields UnspecifiedElements naming the setup`: a snapshot without the experiment's setup yields `UnspecifiedElements` whose reason names `'Setup 1' revision 1`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `the chart and solver-handoff windows leave everything reachable` passes `setups` from `filledExperiments ()`. `WireUiFinalCompositionTests`: `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff` passes `setups = []`. `KitWindowTests` (steps 226, 229): `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit` and `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen` record the source's setup first, their assertions kept. After this step `git grep -n -w -E "ElementDescriptor|ElementBinding|PlacementSummary|VersionRef" -- Berreman/` finds nothing. The retirement of ElementDescriptor MUST also retire its S6 itemIdOpt field; the same assigned ItemIds MUST be carried by SlotContent.ItemInSlot in replacement fixtures, with no second association map, fallback or disk migration. S6 identity, missing-reference and same-preset tests MUST keep their assertions while constructing SetupReferences and SetupSlots. The copy and ToggleCopiedExperiment callers MUST handle the new Result error type and preserve their pre-write refusal behavior. `recommitting a copied experiment preserves its assigned physical ids` MUST retain the copied setup's item assignments after commit/reopen. The S6 experiment-schema identity test MUST be renamed `setup files preserve distinct same-preset physical ids and reject malformed slot identity` and assert the corresponding setup schema, replacing its old descriptor-field assertion in this same step. The copied target's placement/library binding MUST be regenerated from the mapped item when necessary, so a target identity and the slot's rendered binding cannot disagree. The existing S6 rewrite/resolution tests MUST run over the slot representation and MUST not be deleted or weakened. In Kit.fs, SetupError MUST gain SetupItemReferenceErr of ItemError, rendered through the payload describe. Storage MUST wrap this resolver error once with KitLibrarySetupErr. The error remains declared below the identity types in Kit.fs, so Setups.fs has no dependency on the later KitLibrary.fs. SetupTests MUST exercise and render the nested missing-item diagnostic; the S6 missing-item assertion MUST preserve the UnknownKitItemErr payload under this setup-error wrapper. The descriptor consumer ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs MUST remain deleted, with its stale census path included only to preserve that deletion.

**Acceptance.** After experiments reference setups, `Experiment.setup` MUST be a `SetupReference`, `ElementDescriptor`, `ElementBinding`, `PlacementSummary` and `VersionRef` MUST be gone (`git grep -n -w -E "ElementDescriptor|ElementBinding|PlacementSummary|VersionRef" -- Berreman/` finding nothing), a commit MUST record the table as the active setup, minting the next revision when an experiment uses the current one, `recordExperiment` MUST refuse a revision the kit lacks, and a copy MUST bring the setups with their items mapped; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `E1 references its setup revision and names its varied polarizer with its label`, `committing references the setup revision and the varied slot with its label`, `the items an experiment uses are those its setup revision's slots hold, each once`, `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving their setup references, optional shapes and data attachments`, `recording an experiment over a setup revision the kit holds writes its file and snapshots nothing of its own`, `an experiment over a setup revision the kit lacks records nothing`, `a copy brings the setups its experiments reference, their items mapped onto the kit's`, `a copied setup the kit holds with the same content is not written again, and one with other content takes the next free name`, `an experiment pins the revision it references, and its slots resolve through the kit's setups`, `a commit on a table that is no setup yet records it as the first free setup and references it`, `a commit over a changed table whose revision an experiment references mints the next revision, and the earlier experiment keeps its own` and `a commit over a changed table no experiment references changes the setup in place`, the count rising by 1 (seven new facts, six deleted); ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the root window-launcher factory opens and renders Materials, Library, the three editors, and the SolverHandoff`, `pressing Copy experiments, a toggle and Copy brings the experiment into the kit` and `pressing a mapping choice and Copy adds or maps the item as chosen`; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `an experiment whose setup the collection lacks yields UnspecifiedElements naming the setup`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass. The S6 copy tests MUST still resolve the reopened setup slots to the explicitly chosen physical ids and parameters, and missing setup/item identities MUST remain typed failures before writes.
